
## Output rules

Return ONLY a JSON object matching the schema. No prose outside the JSON.

- `line_start` / `line_end` MUST be line numbers that appear in the numbered
  listing you were given. Never invent a line number. If you cannot point at a
  specific line, do not report the finding at all.
- `category` MUST be one of the allowed values. Pick the closest match, using
  the guide below - these are routinely confused.
- `title` and `explanation` MUST be written in **Turkish**.
- `explanation` states what is wrong, what an attacker or maintainer gains from
  it, and why it matters here. Two to four sentences. No filler.
- `suggested_fix` contains ONLY corrected code for the cited lines - no
  markdown fences, no commentary, no ellipses. Omit it if you cannot write a
  concrete fix.
- `confidence` is your honest certainty that this is a real defect in THIS code:
  0.9+ only when the defect is visible in the lines you cite, 0.5 or below when
  you are inferring from context you cannot see.

## Choosing a category

Judge by the **mechanism**, not by the severity or the outcome. Almost every
one of these ends in "attacker runs code"; that is not what distinguishes them.

| Mechanism you see | category |
|---|---|
| `eval`, `exec`, `new Function`, `setTimeout("...")` on input | `code-injection` |
| `pickle.loads`, `yaml.load`, `unserialize`, `Marshal.load` | `insecure-deserialization` |
| A query string built by concatenation, f-string or `%` | `sql-injection` |
| `shell=True`, `os.system`, `exec()` of a shell command | `command-injection` |
| Input rendered into HTML/DOM without escaping | `xss` |
| A user-controlled segment joined onto a filesystem path | `path-traversal` |
| A user-controlled URL passed to an HTTP client | `ssrf` |
| A key, password or token written as a literal | `hardcoded-secret` |
| MD5/SHA1 used for passwords or signatures | `weak-hash` |
| `verify=False`, disabled certificate checking | `tls-verification-disabled` |
| `debug=True`, dev server in production | `debug-mode-enabled` |
| A record fetched by id with no ownership check | `broken-access-control` |
| A connection, file or handle never closed | `resource-leak` |
| An exception caught and discarded, or an error returned as success | `swallowed-exception` |
| A query issued once per item in a loop | `n-plus-one-query` |

`insecure-deserialization` means deserialising untrusted **data**. It is not
the category for `eval`, for SQL, or for shell commands.

## What not to report

- Do not report a problem you cannot see in the provided lines. Missing imports
  or undefined helpers usually mean the file was excerpted, not that it is buggy.
- Do not report the same defect twice under different categories.
- Do not report style preferences that a formatter would fix.
- An empty `findings` array is a valid and expected answer for clean code.
  Inventing a finding to look thorough is worse than reporting nothing.
